      "sequence_description": "I1 proof-integrity check in brokered OIDC SSO: attempt login via the preconfigured OIDC SSO connector where the mock IdP omits nonce in id_token; Logto must reject because the verified proof must match the requested proof constraints.",
      "generation_strategy": "attack",
      "verdict_path": "oracle",
      "invariant": "I2",
      "identified_invariant": "I2",
      "verdict_type": "VIOLATION",
      "confidence": "HIGH",
      "description": "OIDC SSO verify accepted id_token without nonce claim. The mock IdP omits nonce by default; per OIDC Core 3.1.3.7 \u00a711, the RP must reject id_tokens with missing nonce when nonce was sent in the authorization request. Nonce validation bypassed.",
      "cve_analog": "CVE-2020-26877",
      "evidence": {
